      "shloka_number": 6,
      "full_sanskrit": "धेनुकारिष्टहानिष्टकृद्द्वेषिहा केशिहा कंसहृद्वंशिकावादकः ।\nपूतनाकोपकः सूरजाखेलनो बालगोपालकः पातु मां सर्वदा ॥६॥",
      "sandhi_split_sanskrit": "धेनुकारिष्टहा अनिष्टकृत् द्वेषिहा केशिहा कंसहृत् वंशिकावादकः । | पूतनाकोपकः सूरजाखेलनः बालगोपालकः पातु मां सर्वदा ॥६॥",
      "iast_transliteration": "dhenukāriṣṭahāniṣṭakṛddveṣihā keśihā kaṃsahṛdvaṃśikāvādakaḥ |\npūtanākopakaḥ sūrajākhelano bālagopālakaḥ pātu māṃ sarvadā ||6||",
      "meaning_english": "He who destroyed Dhenuka and Arishta, who killed the hateful wrongdoers, who killed Keshi and Kamsa, who plays the flute. He who showed anger to Putana, who played on the banks of Yamuna, the child cowherd—may He protect me always.",
